{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"b9b4aaf4-5bab-4e93-b961-f906d154a8cd","title":"Graphs of y = 2 sin x and y = sin 2x compared"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b9b4aaf4-5bab-4e93-b961-f906d154a8cd","step":{"id":"s1","script":"In y equals two sine x, the outside factor doubles every height. The amplitude is two, while the horizontal spacing stays unchanged.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"first_rule","region":"A1","latex":"y=2\\sin x"},{"op":"equation","id":"first_amp","anchor":{"el":"first_rule","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\text{Amplitude}=2"},{"op":"figure","id":"comparison","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.3,6.7],"y":[-2.6,2.7],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x (radians)","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"stretched","y":"2*sin(x)","domain":[0,6.28318530718]},{"kind":"point","id":"tall_peak","at":{"on":"stretched","x":1.57079632679}},{"kind":"measure","from":[1.57079632679,0],"to":{"at":"tall_peak"},"label":"2"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b9b4aaf4-5bab-4e93-b961-f906d154a8cd","step":{"id":"s2","script":"In y equals sine two x, the inside factor compresses the graph horizontally. Its amplitude remains one; the dashed curve oscillates faster.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"second_rule","anchor":{"el":"first_amp","side":"below","gap":0.15},"latex":"y=\\sin(2x)\\quad\\text{(dashed)}"},{"op":"equation","id":"second_amp","anchor":{"el":"second_rule","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\text{Amplitude}=1"},{"op":"figure","id":"add_fast","on":"comparison","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"compressed","y":"sin(2*x)","domain":[0,6.28318530718],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","id":"short_peak","at":{"on":"compressed","x":0.7853981634}},{"kind":"measure","from":[0.7853981634,0],"to":{"at":"short_peak"},"label":"1"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b9b4aaf4-5bab-4e93-b961-f906d154a8cd","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Compare complete cycles: the solid curve repeats after two pi, but the dashed curve repeats after pi. Doubling the input halves the period.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"period_marks","on":"comparison","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-2.35],"to":[6.28318530718,-2.35],"label":"2π"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,2.4],"to":[3.14159265359,2.4],"label":"π"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"periods","anchor":{"el":"second_amp","side":"below","gap":0.15},"latex":"T_{2\\sin x}=2\\pi,\\qquad T_{\\sin(2x)}=\\pi"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b9b4aaf4-5bab-4e93-b961-f906d154a8cd","step":{"id":"s4","script":"At pi over two, the solid curve reaches two while the dashed curve crosses zero. Outside factors change amplitude; inside factors change period.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"compare_values","on":"comparison","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"fast_zero","at":{"on":"compressed","x":1.57079632679}},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"fast_zero"},"to":{"at":"tall_peak"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[1.9,-0.3],"text":"x = π/2","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"general_rule","anchor":{"el":"periods","side":"below","gap":0.15},"latex":"y=A\\sin(bx):\\quad \\text{amplitude}=|A|,\\quad T=\\frac{2\\pi}{|b|}"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which curve completes two cycles between 0 and 2π?","expected_gist":"The dashed curve y = sin(2x)."}}}
